{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"brattish-ladyish-jaguar","creation_channel":"python","description":"## The defect\n\nBug 7e90-233b-3ee9-4f14 fixed the `Git version floor gate` step, which hard-failed every\nchange branched before its data file landed. The same class of defect is still live in\n`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` on OTHER gate steps that run a repo script with no\nif-present guard.\n\nThe workflow's own \"Definition-vs-tree skew guard (ticket ee2a)\" note states the rule\nverbatim: a gate step that runs a repo script must skip (with a log line) when the script is\nabsent from the checked-out tree. Gerrit's Verified lane takes the workflow DEFINITION from\nthe target branch but checks out the CHANGE'S tree, so a step added on main runs against\nopen changes whose base predates its script.\n\n## Unguarded gate steps (swept from the parsed workflow YAML)\n\nIn `_build-and-test.yml`, which BOTH the Gerrit Verified lane and branch CI run:\n\n| step | script | script first added |\n|---|---|---|\n| `comment-hygiene gate` | `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` | 2026-08-03 |\n| `Config-read gate` | `scripts/check_config_reads.py` | 2026-08-02 |\n| `Verified-gate parity gate` | `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` | 2026-07-19 |\n| `Env-var registry drift gate` | `scripts/gen_env_registry.py` | 2026-07-08 |\n| `Docs-index completeness gate` | `scripts/check_docs_index.py` | 2026-07-11 |\n| `README quickstart golden-path gate` | `scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py` | 2026-07-11 |\n| `CLI-reference drift gate` | `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` | 2026-07-11 |\n| `MCP-reference drift gate` | `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` | 2026-07-11 |\n| `server.json env-contract drift gate` | `scripts/check_server_manifest.py` | 2026-07-04 |\n\nThe two 2026-08-02/03 scripts are the LIVE exposure -- open changes branched before those\ndates exist today. The older ones are the same latent class and should be guarded for\nuniformity, so the next reader does not have to re-derive which are safe.\n\n`gerrit-verify.yaml`'s `golden-path` job also checks out the Gerrit patchset and runs\n`scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py` and `scripts/probe_rebar.py` unguarded -- same class,\nsame lane.\n\n## Confirmed empirically\n\nRunning each unguarded step's command in a directory without the script exits 2 with\n`can't open file '.../scripts/<name>.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory` -- a hard CI\nfailure indistinguishable from a real gate violation, which is exactly what produced the\nfalse Verified -1 in 7e90.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every gate step in `_build-and-test.yml` that runs a repo script carries the ee2a\n      if-present guard, skipping with a log line naming the tree-skew cause.\n- [ ] The `golden-path` job in `gerrit-verify.yaml` is guarded the same way.\n- [ ] A genuine gate violation still fails when the script IS present -- no gate is weakened.\n- [ ] A test (mirroring `tests/unit/test_git_floor_gate_tree_skew.py`) executes each guarded\n      step against a tree lacking the script and asserts it exits 0 without an `::error::`.\n- [ ] Consider a structural guard: a check that FAILS when a step in the Verified lane runs a\n      repo script without the if-present guard, so the convention stops depending on authors\n      remembering the ee2a note.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound by the Step 7 sibling sweep while fixing bug 7e90-233b-3ee9-4f14.\n","id":"1909-c1a7-9f20-440f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Other CI gate steps still hard-fail on the definition-vs-tree skew"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785911752713508001,"uuid":"c35b1ec0-49bc-4909-bd37-77123405d41d"}